de appearance only, not verified material or dimensions.\n<Subject 2> is the adult East Asian heroine in <Picture 2>, with shoulder-length dark hair, an ivory knit top, charcoal trousers and a slim dark belt.\n<Subject 3> is the adult East Asian friend in cell 7 of <Picture 2>, with tied-back dark hair, a pale-blue shirt and dark trousers.\n<Subject 4> is the entryway in <Picture 2>, with a wooden-framed mirror and walnut console on the left, the door on the right, and soft daylight from the left.\n<Picture 2> is a seven-panel shot-planning sheet, not a first-frame anchor. In its four rows, cells 1/2 are top-left/top-right, cells 3/4 second-row-left/right, cells 5/6 third-row-left/right, and cell 7 spans the bottom row. Cells 1-7 correspond respectively to [Shot 1]-[Shot 7], defining compositions and action starting states.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Create a 15-second, 9:16 live-action Chinese product story using <Subject 1> from <Picture 1>, with <Subject 2> preparing to leave <Subject 4> and joining <Subject 3>. <Picture 2> guides the seven-shot sequence. Both sheets are references only: every video shot is one full-screen scene with no grid, panel numbers, collage or generated subtitles.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]-[Shot 7]): fully_preserved - preserve its defined visible caramel surface, rounded silhouette, dark trim, single strap and gold-tone hardware; staging does not establish product size or performance.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]-[Shot 7], hands only in [Shot 2]-[Shot 4]): fully_preserved - retain face, hair, wardrobe and right-shoulder carrying continuity.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 7], heard off-screen in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - retain her appearance and identity.\n<Subject 4> (appears in [Shot 1]-[Shot 7], close-up fragments in [Shot 3]-[Shot 4]): fully_preserved - retain furniture placement and daylight direction.\n<Picture 2> ([Shot 1]-[Shot 7] planning): partially_preserved - retain panel-to-shot order and action states, adapt each composition to a full-screen 9:16 frame and remove all grid lines and numbers.\n\ndetailed_description:\nUse naturalistic live-action photography, restrained warm color and soft left daylight. Each shot fills the vertical frame. Preserve the bag color, rounded outline and single strap; never reveal unverified inner pockets or rear construction.\n\n[Shot 1] A static medium view follows cell 1 of <Picture 2>. <Subject 2> stands beside the mirror in <Subject 4>, studying her reflection before glancing toward <Subject 1> on the console. <Subject 3> (S1), off-screen near the door, asks in a bright adult female Mandarin voice, <d>[Chinese] 好了没？</d> The heroine's lips remain closed.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the camera cuts to the bag's unobstructed front on the console, following cell 2. Push in slowly with small amplitude as the heroine's right hand contacts its strap without lifting the body. <Subject 2> (S2), with a warm conversational adult female Mandarin voice, says in an off-screen voiceover: <d>[Chinese] 差一只包。</d> Her lips remain closed and outside the frame.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.000, the camera cuts to the caramel front surface and dark piping, following cell 3. Truck slowly a short distance as her right fingertips gently stroke the front, ending beside the trim. The bag stays on the console. <Subject 2> (S2) says in an off-screen voiceover: <d>[Chinese] 焦糖棕，哑光绒面。</d> Her lips remain closed and outside the frame.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:06.000, the camera cuts to a static top close-up following repaired cell 4. Her left hand steadies the left rim; her right thumb and index finger hold the single brown zipper pull near the right endpoint. Pull the slider toward viewer-right until the short remaining gap closes. Keep the interior concealed and one slider only. A zipper sound accompanies closure. <Subject 2> (S2) says in an off-screen voiceover: <d>[Chinese] 拉上，出门。</d> Her lips remain closed and outside the frame.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:09.